ay it is 32 percent  and if we see 18 000 people a day coming  across the border  then we're going to see those numbers  sink even lower  i loved it jen pasake said it's the  federal government's responsibility to  enforce the immigration laws not the  states so therefore he can't do it well  when is the federal government going to  start enforcing the law the state of  texas is spending  millions of dollars  every week in order to fill the gaps on  the border that the border patrol openly  says we don't have enough resources  technology and people demand i spent the  last weekend with the father of one of  the national guardsmen deployed to the  border his son is telling them that  every night his squad is out there all  night long with night vision goggles and  heavily armed and they take fire from  across the river the mexican cartels  shoot tracers in order to make certain  that their appearance is known and every  night they are picking up dozens of  illegals and they're in one very small  stretch maybe a couple of miles long on  the on the border and though our border  with text with mexico is hundreds of  miles long so this is a grave crisis for  the country and the non-shallot attitude  of of the white house jen posaki as she  gets ready to leave for cable tv news is  like we're in charge don't worry about  it we got it handled and they do not  have it handled and it's going to come  back to bottom big time in the election  i wanted to ask you about that carl just  the political calculation as well so the  white house can count they can see  what's happening to their poll numbers  on this but they seem to be making a  different calculation so i know that the  left-wing immigration groups that really  wanted title 42 to be lifted must they  must be very persuasive so when when  when the prime minister as i call him  ron claim the chief of staff is as as  they look at this maybe they think one  lifting it is the right thing to do on  the merits but there's something it  tells me that president biden wouldn't  necessarily have done this in his  previous you know position as a senator  he might have been one of those that had  been a co-sponsor to keep it  yeah  that's very interesting inside very very  key one because remember what the  progressives are saying or the  progressive caucus in the house and  progressive senators in the senate is  the reason your numbers are low is that  you aren't doing enough in pursuit of  progressive goals so they don't you know  that you haven't you you've got 42 of  title 42 still in place you will get  better paypal said pass bill back better  and do and put the 71 executive orders  including the the  the ending of title 42  prohibitions at the border and democrats  will gain seats in the congress so the  mindset of the progressives is  you've got to do these weird things like  get rid of title 42 and and end student  debt all together and make these other  changes that we can't get passed through  law and executive order and that will  cause democrat enthusiasm to rise and  we'll have a good election in the fall i  think it's nutty and obviously so do  senators in places like new hampshire  and arizona and elsewhere who are in  hotly contested races  remember that says cdc were going to go  in their guidance a week ago right now  fauci fauci has had double speak in  three weeks carl in 21 days he's seen it  but he's seen both sides of these issues  coming up in the fall so thank you so  much we'll see what happens then karl  rove thanks in texas

